; C9  Winning 42 pp. 39-40 (W42-p040-b, W42-p040-c, W42-p040-d); played in
; Hands 29, 30 and 31 (pp. 101, 103, 107)
; Rule, in our words: the bidder's partner on lead never leads trump. Among his
; other tiles he leads one that cannot draw count; failing that, one that can
; draw only a five; a ten-count suit last.
; Python gate (pour_bidder gate_c9, "never trump"): partner on lead holding
; trump and a non-trump; the book's tiles are the non-trumps. The ordering is a
; second, narrower gate in the same function.
; How this encoding differs: it writes "never trump" in full; the ordering is
; not written (GAP none). The book's own exception (every other lead calls a
; ten) is in neither.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0, the partner as S2.
; GAP none: "a tile whose suit has no count still out" is a negated existential
; (no live count tile outside the hand follows that suit), and the ordering
; needs it.
(policy c09-partner-never-leads-trump
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule lead-anything-but-trump (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (domino lead) (domino trump))
        (out lead)
        (pattern
          (viewer S2)
          (leader S2)
          (next-actor S2)
          (own-legal lead)
          (not (in lead q*))
          (own-legal trump)
          (in trump q*))))))
